# devices/dodge/drivers/wifi/conf: the Wi-Fi drivers of this phone (docs/drivers-config.md).
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in configs/dodge_defconfig builds one in; tools/hakios-config.py reads this file.
# The `file` lines are also what the legacy build follows: the file next to this conf is copied
# to that path in the XNU tree (the .github workflow does it; the names are the tree's own).

driver WCN
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.wcn.c
	help    the WCN7850 radio's PCIe bring-up, in stages (wifi_pcie=N: 1 read-only probe, 2 WLAN_EN and
	help    the GDSCs, ... 7 the endpoint's config space); also probes the CPUCP's SCMI mailbox, the way
	help    in to the clock controller this VM's gcc window is filtered. Not a network driver: bring-up only
